<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-17870] SQL. Do not yield separate query result for comments</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-17870</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Motivation&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently, lines with commented out lines yield additional query result. For the query below, three results will be returned (result for comment is &#8220;updated rows: 0&#8220;). You can play with the comments position within the entire query, the behavior with comments is not consistent and clear.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;#8211; asdf&lt;br/&gt;
SELECT * FROM Test_Person limit 1;&lt;br/&gt;
update Test_Person set name=&apos;sdfsdf&apos; where id = 44444444;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;#8211; come&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;#8211; asdf&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What to do&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do not yield a separate query result for commented out lines.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
